WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.490
<i>Damn...</i>

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.000
Damn!

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.490
It is mine!
You won't have it!

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.800
Just try and take it from me!

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:11.600
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:19.050
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.960
Treasure
Island

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.760
Takarajima

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.570
saa ikou

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.570
Come, let's go

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.660
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.660
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.500
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.500
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.380
umi hedeyou

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.380
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.300
ikute ni wa

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.300
Many of us

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.300
minna mada shiranai

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.300
Still don't know of

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.050
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.050
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.550
matte iru darou

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.550
That await us there

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.060
itsumo shinji you

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.060
We must always have trust

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.310
magokoro wo

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.310
And be sincere

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.570
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.570
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.700
tade hitotsu no

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.700
I only...

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.120
akogare dake wa

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.120
...have one desire

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.410
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.410
And no one...

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.120
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.120
...will ever take it away

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.670
tade hitotsu no

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.670
I only...

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.970
akogare dake wa

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.970
...have one desire

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.300
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.300
And no one...

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.230
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.230
...will ever take it away

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.020
episode

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.020
Billy the terrible
\h    has arrived!

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.370
The Admiral Benbow Inn

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.290
Just moments ago,
I heard someone cry.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.070
It sounded like they're in pain, suffering...

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.490
It was very frightening!

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.590
It wasn't just the sound of waves?

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.930
Evening storms make that happen a lot.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.480
That could be it, but I am sure
that I heard voices...

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.570
Well, it's time to close the inn, Jim.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.070
It'll surprise me if we get
customers on a night like this.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.300
Alright, I'll go turn off the lantern.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.280
Thank you.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.020
M-Mother, we have a customer!

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.150
Welcome!

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.110
The Admiral Benbow Inn...
That name pleases me.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.410
Hey, lad, bring my chest inside.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.650
I don't want it left out in the rain.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.560
Yes, sir.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.030
I want some rum!

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.250
Bring me a whole bottle!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.520
Coming up.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.120
What terrible weather, don't you think...

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.440
That hits the spot.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.020
There.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.660
The cape is nearby, and so is the creek...

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.800
And what's perfect is that
you're outside the village.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.630
Do you have any other customers?

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.010
No, none.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.220
Very good...
This place is perfect.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.260
This is the home for me.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.230
Give me the key to my room.
I'll stay here.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.500
Here's an advanced payment.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.690
That'll prevent me from spending it.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.650
<i>Wow!
Real pieces of gold!</i>

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:51.620
Lad!
Bring up my stuff.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.570
Yes, sir, I'm on it!

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.580
Excuse me, sir, can you
give me your name?

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.060
"Captain!"

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.960
Captain...
Put me down as "Captain".

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.560
<i>This is a heavy sea chest.</i>

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.890
<i>It belonged to a strange man,
who arrived on a stormy night...</i>

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.400
<i>My father died a month earlier
and my mother and I had to...</i>

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.360
<i>...take care of the inn ourselves.</i>

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.700
It's okay, mother.
I can do it!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.320
<i>But geez, this thing is heavy...</i>

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.920
Here's your chest.
Where should I put it?

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.550
Put it beside my bed.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.460
Yes, sir!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:07:01.690
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:09.600
Yo-ho-ho!
And a bottle of rum.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.500
<i>My name is Jim.
Jim Hawkins.</i>

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.370
<i>I was born in Black Hill,
a small village of England.</i>

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.820
<i>I am 13 years old.</i>

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.500
<i>But already a man!</i>

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.650
<i>And this is my friend Benbow.</i>

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:39.000
<i>He's a leopard cub that was given to me by a customer on his return from Africa.</i>

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:58.690
<i>It's been a month since my father was taken from my mother and me by an illness.</i>

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:00.530
<i>"I would love to return to the sea."</i>

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.720
<i>How many times had I heard
my father repeat that phrase?</i>

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.590
Hi, hello!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.250
Did you see that storm, yesterday night?

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.350
Did the roof of the inn hold up?

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.930
Obviously.
It was only a small storm after all!

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.730
Enough about that.
Here, look at this.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:31.970
I went to the village and bought this to prepare dinner for our customer.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.530
That's great, Jim.
So you have a customer?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.200
Of course, Lilly!

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.130
Our Admiral Benbow Inn...

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.450
...will regain its prosperity of yore!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.100
You're working hard, aren't you, Jim?
Both you and your mother.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:51.450
It's a given that we work hard!

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.850
Benbow, let's go.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.600
See you later, Jim!

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.770
See you later!

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:05.830
Goodbye!

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.690
Goodbye!

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:11.100
<i>I don't have time for fun.</i>

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.990
<i>Why? Because I have to help my mother with the inn.</i>

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.610
<i>Especially now that we have a customer.</i>

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:19.450
I'm back!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:25.290
Excuse me, for being... a little late.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.290
Thanks for the effort.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.090
Now, please wash the floor, okay?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:30.760
Okay.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:39.010
"We finally have a customer..."

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:45.770
Jim!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.020
Our customer has gone to bed again.
Try to be a bit more quiet.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.840
Oops, my bad...

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.590
Lad, is this the only exit
on this floor?

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:19.350
Yes, that's the only one.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:21.650
Alright...

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.510
Lad!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:24.080
Yes, sir!

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.930
Did anyone ask to see me?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.480
No, no one.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.690
I see...
That's good to hear, yeah.

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:39.110
<i>Our inn doesn't only welcome travelers,
we also serve booze.</i>

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:43.640
<i>So at night, the people of the village
come to drink with us...</i>

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.330
<i>...and the place gets very busy.</i>

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.610
Mother, three beers, please!

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:51.750
Coming up.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:58.170
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...!

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.630
Yo-ho-ho...!

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:05.320
Come on, sing with me!

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:11.270
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:15.230
Come on, sing!
Sing, instead of yakking!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.190
Sing!
Sing, sailors!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:25.580
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.500
Yo-ho-ho...!

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.160
Oi, landlubbers!
Why aren't you singing!?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:56.610
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.580
Yo-ho-ho—

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:05.660
...and a bottle of rum...

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.220
<i>We really have an odd customer.</i>

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.580
<i>A rumour is spreading
throughout the village...</i>

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:20.890
<i>...that a pirate has chosen
our inn to be his dwelling.</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.060
<i>Suddenly, the villagers don't come anymore,</i>

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.270
<i>and things aren't going very well.</i>

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.640
Gathering firewood, are you, Jim?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:34.890
Yup.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:43.030
You must see Dr. Livesey and talk to him about that pirate.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.940
We're not sure if he's a pirate.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.830
We have no proof!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.250
Does he pay his rent regularly?

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.670
At first he did.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.340
But...

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.140
<i>What? The rent?</i>

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:04.820
<i>Yeah, there's nothing left
of our three pieces of gold.</i>

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.100
<i>Paying every single day is such a bother...</i>

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.300
<i>I understand, but...</i>

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:11.100
<i>Alright, I get it!</i>

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.230
<i>Put it all on my bill!
The bill!</i>

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.580
<i>I will pay it all at once when I leave this place. That should do.</i>

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.280
<i>Deal with it!</i>

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:26.240
I also think you should go see Dr. Livesey.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.900
Don't worry.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:32.660
When you run an inn,
you must trust the customers.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.610
Let's go, Benbow!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:39.130
He should get advice from Dr. Livesey.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:05.530
<i>I still couldn't trust him.</i>

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.490
<i>If he really is a pirate, that would be terrible!</i>

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:21.070
<i>There were three things
that made me suspicious.</i>

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.060
<i>Firstly, when he was drunk,</i>

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:27.540
<i>he sang the same song
the whole time.</i>

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:29.930
<i>That one, about the "dead man's chest".</i>

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:35.890
<i>Secondly, he spends his time on the cliff
scanning the surroundings.</i>

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.440
<i>And third, that treasured chest of his!</i>

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.860
<i>He keeps a close eye on it.</i>

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.170
<i>He always keeps it closed.
I've never seen him open it.</i>

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:55.620
Good night, papa.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.630
Doctor Livesey!

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.300
You okay, Jim?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.470
I've heard things about your customer
and I'm a little worried.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.020
Welcome back, Doctor Livesey.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.300
It's really been a long time.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:27.060
Yes, you see, this time I was in London.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:28.860
That's why I was gone for so long.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.490
Hey, Jim.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.490
My bottle is empty,
bring me another one.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:34.810
Yes, right away.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.460
<i>So, that's him?
I see... yes.</i>

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.040
Thanks for waiting.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.490
Yeah, sure.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.580
Hey, you over there!
Come drink with me.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.340
It's glum drinking all alone.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.330
We will sing together.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:01.440
Fifteen men on a dead...

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.140
Oi, ye scurvy landlubber!

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:12.610
Why aren't you singing?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.890
Stop here for a moment.

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:23.290
Isn't that Doctor Livesey's horse?

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.540
Yes, it <i>is</i> his.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:29.920
Has he returned from London already?

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:38.670
Hey, landlubber, are you deaf?!
I was telling you to sing!

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:42.480
Who's this landlubber you speak of?
Could you perchance mean myself?

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.060
Obviously.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.640
Do you see any other man in this inn?

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.780
It looks like the rum
has affected your brain.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.450
Continue to drink like this and your life will soon be forfeit.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.530
What?

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:00.040
I am Dr. Livesey.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:04.680
I have known many men who abuse
alcohol and become violent like you.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:08.630
Next thing you know,
they end up six feet under.

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:10.960
What do you know about me, cur?!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.560
That's enough!
I'm not just a doctor!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:19.350
Know that I am the magistrate
of the county as well!

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.680
M-Magistrate?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.660
Magistrate?

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:27.700
That's right!

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.620
If I learn that you make
a scene like this again,

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:35.570
I will immediately arrest you
and throw you in prison!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.290
Listen closely!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.660
Now that I know there is an individual like this in my county,

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.240
you can be sure that I will keep an eye on you day and night!

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:52.440
Alright! I understand.
God damn it...

00:17:54.900 --> 00:18:00.140
In any case, I think that from now on,
he will pay you without a fuss.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:01.390
Doctor Livesey!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.700
I don't know how to thank you.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.430
It was nothing...

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:10.470
My congratulations to you,
magistrate, sir!

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:13.320
I must say that
I was a little scared.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.780
{Squire}Mr. Trelawney!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.500
That was unbelievable, Jim.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.740
Thanks to him, the people of the village
will soon return.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:28.260
<i>{Squire}Mr. Trelawney is a very rich man and the most powerful in the village.</i>

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.840
<i>As for Dr. Livesey, he is also
the magistrate of our county.</i>

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:36.490
<i>They had both been friends of my late father ever since they were little.</i>

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.060
<i>Who are you looking for?</i>

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.220
<i>What is it that worries you so much?</i>

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:58.240
<i>He's been here everyday.</i>

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:13.920
Avast!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.340
Come back, lad!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.360
Avast!

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.120
Lad!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:35.500
Lad, who asked you to follow me?

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.420
That skirt wearing magistrate?

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.400
You're wrong!

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:41.590
No one asked me to do anything!
It was my own idea!

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.950
Really, it was your idea?
Then, why?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.740
Because I find you suspicious!

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.950
I think that you're a pirate!

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:55.880
Yer honest, lad...
and brave!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:00.250
Come and get me!
I'm not afraid of you!

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:04.300
Mama!

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:07.460
Let me go, let me go!

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:08.380
Let me go!

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:09.770
Let me go!

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:14.470
Oi, your name's Jim, right?

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.730
Y-Yes.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:20.700
You are a man now.
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:21.650
A favor?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.780
Yes.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.790
I want you to warn me
if you see a sailor with one leg.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.820
<i>A sailor with one leg?</i>

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:40.090
<i>If you see or hear about him,
come warn me immediately.</i>

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:45.780
<i>Who's this one-legged sailor?
Why him?</i>

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.350
<i>It's best that you don't know.</i>

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:57.130
<i>In any case, beware of him.
He is very dangerous.</i>

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:05.420
<i>Take this, Jim.
It's your salary.</i>

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:08.660
<i>I will pay you four pence a day.
That's not bad, right?</i>

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.810
No one has touched it.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.660
I won't let anyone take it.
It's mine.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:44.620
The treasure will be mine.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.650
<i>A treasure...
A sailor with one leg...</i>

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.240
<i>So many...</i>

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.740
<i>So many things that
I don't understand, but...</i>

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:10.550
<i>Geez, that guy's bad news!</i>

00:22:12.090 --> 00:22:13.890
<i>How am I supposed to sleep tonight?</i>

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:27.410
To      be        continued

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:33.490
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:33.490
Hey sea breeze

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:39.300
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:39.300
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:45.510
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:45.510
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:50.950
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:50.950
A word to my dear mother

00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:56.360
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:56.360
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:22:56.360 --> 00:23:01.820
kaban ippai no

00:22:56.360 --> 00:23:01.820
And that my bag filled

00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:07.450
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:01.820 --> 00:23:07.450
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:07.450 --> 00:23:13.310
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:07.450 --> 00:23:13.310
Will be brought back

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:19.900
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:19.900
The sunset on my back

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:25.790
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:25.790
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:35.510
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:35.510
I blow out a whistle

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:44.520
An "old friend" of Captain Billy Bones
comes to our inn next time.

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:47.300
But the captain doesn't seem to like him much.

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:49.990
A swordfight begins between the two men.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:53.280
To make matters worse,
the captain suddenly faints.

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:54.920
As his caregiver,

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:57.580
I learn a little more about him.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:24:00.970
Does this old friend have a connection with the famous one-legged man?

00:24:01.570 --> 00:24:04.520
